 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Delivery behavior
+
+Each subscribed event creates one delivery for the webhook and is POSTed once. The request body is the event as JSON for generic endpoints. Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp receivers get the corresponding message payload wrapper. Requests have an `application/json` content type, an `X-Webhook-Timestamp` set to the event time, and an `X-Webhook-Signature` containing the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the request body using the webhook's signing secret. Delivery records expose the request and response outcome without exposing the signature.
+
+A webhook is deactivated after 10 consecutive failed deliveries in a one-hour window. Reactivating it starts a new failure sequence. Delivery history is retained for seven days.
diff --git a/test/models/webhook/delinquency_tracker_test.rb b/test/models/webhook/delinquency_tracker_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f7a270a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/models/webhook/delinquency_tracker_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class Webhook::DelinquencyTrackerTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
+  setup do
+    @webhook = webhooks(:active)
+    @tracker = Webhook::DelinquencyTracker.create_or_find_by!(webhook: @webhook)
+  end
+
+  test "deactivates a webhook after ten consecutive failures within an hour" do
+    travel_to Time.current.change(usec: 0) do
+      9.times { @tracker.record_failure }
+
+      assert @webhook.reload.active?
+      assert_equal 9, @tracker.reload.consecutive_failures_count
+
+      @tracker.record_failure
+
+      assert_not @webhook.reload.active?
+      assert_equal 10, @tracker.reload.consecutive_failures_count
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "a successful delivery resets the failure sequence" do
+    3.times { @tracker.record_failure }
+
+    @tracker.record_success
+    @tracker.reload
+
+    assert_equal 0, @tracker.consecutive_failures_count
+    assert_nil @tracker.first_failure_at
+  end
+
+  test "failures outside the one hour window start a new sequence" do
+    travel_to 2.hours.ago do
+      9.times { @tracker.record_failure }
+    end
+
+    @tracker.record_failure
+    @tracker.reload
+
+    assert_equal 1, @tracker.consecutive_failures_count
+    assert @webhook.reload.active?
+  end
+
+  test "reactivating a webhook resets its failure sequence" do
+    10.times { @tracker.record_failure }
+
+    @webhook.reload.activate
+    @tracker.reload
+
+    assert @webhook.active?
+    assert_equal 0, @tracker.consecutive_failures_count
+    assert_nil @tracker.first_failure_at
+  end
+end
diff --git a/test/models/webhook/delivery_test.rb b/test/models/webhook/delivery_test.rb
